{{skl|Fishing}} is one of the core player [[Skills]] in SkyBlock. Mainly, it can be leveled up by catching items such as [[Treasure]] or [[Trophies]] or slaying [[Sea Creatures]]. Players can fish in either {{Item|Water}} or {{Item|Lava}}, each with unique pools, but requiring a different [[Fishing Rod]].

When '''Fishing''', players' catch is determined by several rolls. In order they are:
#[[Sea Creatures]], chance of which is equal to their {{stat|SCC}}. Sea Creatures have a numerical value called "[[Sea Creatures#Weight|Weight]]", which determines the odds of each Sea Creature and can be increased by various sources. 
#[[Trophies]], chance of which varies depending on Trophy and is increased by {{stat|Trophy Chance}}. Specific Trophy and their tier is rolled from the rarest to the most common.
#[[Treasure]], chance of which is equal to their {{stat|Treasure Chance}}. {{InfoNeeded|Details about which determines the tier of treasure and which specific treasure is caught.}}

== Fishing ==
=== Fishing Speed ===
{{Main|Fishing Speed}}

{{stat|Fishing Speed}} decreases the amount of time it takes the player to catch an item or Sea Creature. 

Fishing Speed Cap defaults to 300, but varies on some islands.
