=== Sea Creatures ===
{{Main|Sea Creatures}}

When fishing, players have a chance to catch a [[Sea Creatures|Sea Creature]]. Sea Creatures are mobs which drop Fishing loot and Fishing XP when killed. The player's {{Stat|scc}} determines the chance they have to catch a Sea Creature and {{Stat|dhc}} determines the chance of fishing two Sea Creatures at once.

As a player increases their fishing level, they unlock stronger creatures that give more XP and better loot. Killing sea creatures on the private island does not provide fishing XP. 

Sea Creatures cannot be damaged with arrows directly, except those shot from {{Item|Prismarine Bow}}.

[[Runic Mob|Runic]] sea creatures have a 50% chance to drop a Wake Rune upon death. 

Players can disable catching Sea Creatures by wearing at least 2 pieces of {{Item|Bronze Hunter Armor}} or of any of its upgrades, or by using {{Item|Treasure Hook}}. 

=== Trophy Fishing ===
{{Main|Trophy Frogs|Trophy Fish}}
[[Trophies]] can be occasionally caught while fishing on the {{zone|Lotus Atoll}} and {{zone|Crimson Isle}}. {{Stat|Trophy Chance}} increases chances to catch [[Trophies]].

There are multiple tiers of each [[Trophy]] Fish: {{DG|'''Bronze'''}}, {{Gray|'''Silver'''}}, {{Gold|'''Gold'''}}, and {{Cyan|'''Diamond'''}}. [[Trophies]] can exchanged with {{NPCSprite|Researcher Ribery}} or {{NPCSprite|Odger}} for {{Item|Lotus}} or {{Item|Magmafish}}.

Catching individual tiers of [[Trophies]] increases the player's Trophy Fishing level, granting them rewards from {{NPCSprite|Researcher Ribery}} and {{NPCSprite|Odger}}. Additionally, reaching [[Novice Trophy Fisher|Novice]] and [[Adept Trophy Fisher]] unlocks the {{MobSprite|Thunder}} and {{MobSprite|Lord Jawbus}} [[Sea Creatures]].

Players can disable catching Trophies by wearing {{Item|Tera Shell Necklace}}, or by using {{Item|Treasure Hook}}.

=== Treasure Fishing ===
{{Main|Treasure}}

Items can be obtained from fishing if the player does not catch a Sea Creature, depending on their {{Stat|Treasure Chance}}.

There is a base chance of {{Green|89%}} for a {{Catch|good}}, {{Green|10%}} for a {{Catch|great}}, and {{Green|1%}} for an {{Catch|outstanding}}. The chance for great and outstanding catches can be increased using {{Item|Blessed Bait}}, the {{Ench|Blessing}} enchantment, and a {{Rare}} or better {{Item|Hermit Crab Pet}}.
=== Fishing Rods ===
{{Main|Fishing Rods}}

[[Fishing Rods]] are the main tools that player uses to fish. First one can be obtained from {{NPCSprite|Fisherwoman Enid}}, crafted or bought from {{NPCSprite|Fishing Merchant}}.
=== Rod Parts ===
{{Main|Rod Parts}}

Rod Parts come in three variants: Hooks, Lines, and Sinkers. Hooks affect the chance to catch certain items or Sea Creatures, Lines grant global stat bonuses, and Sinkers grant Fishing Rods miscellaneous special abilities.
=== Fishing Baits ===
{{Main|Fishing Bait}}

Baits provide a variety of bonus effects to Fishing. They're consumed when catching something. If the player pulls their rod without catching anything, bait is not consumed. Players can reduce the chance for Bait to be consumed. Using bait is automatic, but can be disabled in the player's [[Bait Sack]].

=== Hotspots ===
{{Main|Fishing Hotspots}}
Once the they're introduced to the concept by {{NPCSprite|Hattie}}, players will be able to find [[Fishing Hotspots|Hotspots]] on most islands that allow fishing, in which player can fish unique [[Sea Creatures#Hotspot|Hotspot Sea Creatures]] and gain minor stat boost.

