== Tips ==
{{Main|Tutorial:Fishing_Guide}}
*There are two main reasons to fish, for the XP and for valuable drops. No matter which is being gone for, it is required to have as much {{stat|fs}} as possible. When fishing for XP, getting as much {{stat|fishing_wisdom}} as possible is recommended. When fishing for valuable drops (from Sea Creatures), getting as much {{stat|scc}} and {{stat|mf}} as possible is recommended. If possible, use the {{Item|Whale Bait}}, which is currently the best bait. If it is too expensive, {{Item|Glowy Chum Bait}} or {{Item|Fish Bait}} serve well as a cheaper alternative.

== Trivia ==
* There are currently 5 [[Fairy Souls]] that can only be obtained by fishing. Two of them can only be fished up in the [[Fairy Grotto]].
* The [[Fishing Crystal]] that spawns with the pond island grants more frequent drops of [[Prismarine Shard]]s and [[Prismarine Crystals]].
* Daytime occurs between 6:00 am–7:00 pm whilst Night time occurs between 7:00 pm–6:00 a.m. It is also indicated by the sun or moon next to the time in the sidebar.
* The Combat XP buffs from [[Slayer]], [[Combat XP Boost Potion]], [[Viking's Tear]], or [[Accessories]] like [[Hunter Ring]] apply to Fishing XP earned from killing sea creatures. {{confirm}}
* XP from Sea Creatures based on Zombies ([[Sea Walker]], [[Monster of the Deep]], [[Water Hydra]]) count for [[Zombie Slayer]]. Similarly, [[Lava Flame|Lava Flames]], the only Blaze Sea Creature, count for [[Blaze Slayer]].
* The chicken of the [[Monster of the Deep]] drops more XP. But for a Runic [[Monster of the Deep]] only killing the Zombie yields a rune. {{confirm}}
* Spooky fishing mobs can be caught whenever the [[Fear Mongerer]] is in the hub, not just during the spooky festival.
